Mineral names and classification reports — IMA-CNMNC (@mp-ima: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mp-sources) { r_1B4ZWGSZKGP6JM3NKPY0D5RJXH
International Mineralogical Association, Commission on New Minerals, Nomenclature and Classification. [Official reports, groups, mineral-name lists, and dated updates](https://cnmnc.units.it/index.php).

Consult the identified edition of the mineral-name list and the full group/nomenclature report relevant to a classification. Distinguish species, groups, varieties, discredited names, and revised definitions. A specimen label from an older collection or an elemental analysis does not alone establish conformity to a current species definition.

The official site provides dated updates and access to publications. Preserve each report/list's authors, date, status, and actual rights; no general open-adaptation licence is inferred. Official identity, report categories, and revision process checked on 29 October 2026. No list is bulk-ingested, and no fixed count of approved minerals is asserted.

**Return:** [Mineralogy and petrology sources — books, laboratories, analytical methods, and research](../Sources.lingua#r_38Q6Z3J7ER2G1B441JXJ14NV5A).
